$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4′-Phenoxybiphenyl-2-carbaldehyde. 4-Phenoxyphenylboronic acid (1.2865 g,
6 mmol, 1 equiv), 2-bromobenzaldehyde (700 μL, 6 mmol, 1 equiv), and
aqueous 2 M Na2CO3 (6 mL, 12 mmol, 2 equiv) reacted in the presence of
PdCl2 (118.4 mg, 0.60 mmol, 0.10 equiv) and PPh3 (480.6 mg, 1.80 mmol,
0.30 equiv) while dissolved in 30 mL of DMF. The reaction was stirred at
110 °C for 5 min before purification via column chromatography
(ether/hexane). The desired product as a white solid (1.5236 g, 93%). mp
69-71 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.07-7.14 (m, 4 H), 7.17 (tt, J =
7.40, 1.13 Hz, 1 H), 7.32-7.44 (m, 4 H), 7.44-7.54 (m, 2 H), 7.65 (td, J
= 7.53, 1.51 Hz, 1 H), 8.03 (ddd, J = 7.78, 1.52, 0.75 Hz, 1 H), 10.04
(d, J = 0.75 Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 118.3, 119.4, 123.9,
127.7, 127.7, 129.9, 130.8, 131.5, 132.4, 133.6, 133.8, 145.3, 156.6,
157.8, 192.4; HRMS (CI) m/z calcd for C19H14O2 [M + NH4] 292.1338, found
292.1344.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
