$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure for Step III:S3 A mixture of 2-bromopyridine (2 mmol), boronic
acid (3 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (6.8 mg, 1.5 mol %), K3PO4·7H2O (1.35 g, 4 mmol)
in mixture of isopropanol (10 mL) and water (10 mL) was stirred at 80°C
for overnight. The mixture was added to brine (40 mL) and extracted four
times with ethyl acetate (25 mL x 4), the solvent was evaporated under
reduced pressure and the product was isolated by short column
chromatography using PE and EA as eluent. (288 mg, 92%). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 8.70 (d, J = 4.7 Hz, 1H), 8.01 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.71 (d, J =
3.8 Hz, 2H), 7.49-7.45 (m, 2H), 7.44-7.37 (m, 1H), 7.20 (dd, J = 8.7, 4.6
Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 157.28, 149.51, 139.17, 136.61,
128.82, 128.61, 128.50, 126.76, 121.96, 120.41.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
